   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the town of Kent to offer an optional twenty year retirement plan to a certain police officer employed by such town",
    "basePrintNo": "A10629",
    "basePrintNoStr": "A10629-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:A10629\n\nTITLE  OF  BILL:    An  act  to  authorize  the town of Kent to offer an\noptional twenty  year  retirement  plan  to  a  certain  police  officer\nemployed by such town\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL: Authorizes the Town of Kent to offer an\noptional  twenty  year retirement plan to Jerry R. Raneri, a Kent police\nofficer.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:  Section 1: The Town of Kent is  author-\nized  to  make  the participation in the optional twenty year retirement\nplan, established pursuant to section 384-d of the retirement and social\nsecurity law, available to Jerry R. Raneri, a police officer employed by\nthe Town of Kent.\n\nSection 2: All employer costs associated with the  implication  of  this\nprovision shall be borne by the Town of Kent.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  This  legislation is necessary to allow the Town of Kent\nto make participation in plan 354-d of the  New  York  State  and  Local\nPolice  and  Fire Retirement System available to police officer Jerry R.\nRaneri.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY: This is new legislation.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: Costs to the Town of Kent.\n\n* Fiscal Note- If the legislation is enacted during the 2010 legislative\nsession, there will be an increase of 54,200 in annual contributions  of\nthe  Town  of Kent for the fiscal year ending March 31, 2011. There will\nbe an immediate past service cost of approximately $29,100 that will  be\nborne  by  the Town of Kent as a one-time payment. The estimate is based\non the assumption that the payment will be made  on  February  1,  2011.\nthis  estimate,  dated  December 21, 2009 was prepared by an actuary for\nthe New York State and Local Employees' Retirement System.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
